{title: 570 - Not I, But Christ}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, be honored, loved, [Eb]exalted;
[Eb]Not I, but Christ, be seen, be [Bb7/D]known, [Eb]be [Bb]heard;
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, in every look and action,
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, [Eb]in [Ab]every [Eb/Bb]thought [Bb]and [Eb]word.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, to gently soothe [Eb]in sorrow,
[Eb]Not I, but Christ, to wipe the [Bb7/D]falling [Bb]tear;
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, to lift the weary burden,
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, [Eb]to [Ab]hush [Eb/Bb]away all [Bb]fear.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Christ, only [Bb7/F]Christ! No idle words [Eb]e'er falling,
[Eb]Christ, only Christ; no needless [Bb7/D]bustling [Bb]sound;
[Eb]Christ, only [Bb7/F]Christ, no self important bearing;
[Eb]Christ, only [Bb7/F]Christ, [Eb]no [Ab]trace [Eb/Bb]of [Bb7]"I" [Eb/Bb]be [Bb]found.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7/F]Christ, my every [Eb]need supplying,
[Eb]Not I, but Christ, my strength and [Bb7/D]health [Eb]to [Bb]be;
[Eb]Christ, only [Bb7/F]Christ, for body, soul, and spirit,
[Eb]Christ, only [Bb7/F]Christ, [Eb]here [Ab]and [Eb/Bb]eternally.
